              "text": "clārus is inherited, usually traced to Proto-Indo-European klh1ros, \"clear, bright\", from kelh1-, \"to call, to shout\" (EtymDB 2.1): it may first have meant \"loud\", like clāmō, \"to shout\" (Lewis & Short). English clear comes from clārus through French."
